summary:
Same characters typed into two heredocs. The only difference is a pair of quotes around the delimiter.
$ cat > unquoted.js <<EOF
const re = new RegExp("Desktop\\/(\\w+)");
console.log(String(re));
EOF

$ cat > quoted.js <<'EOF'
const re = new RegExp("Desktop\\/(\\w+)");
console.log(String(re));
EOF

$ diff unquoted.js quoted.js
1c1
< const re = new RegExp("Desktop\/(\w+)");
---
> const re = new RegExp("Desktop\/(\w+)");

$ node unquoted.js
/Desktop\/(w+)/
$ node quoted.js
/Desktop\/(\w+)/

